cfg←config pairs;st;pair;name;value
⍝ Create a configuration object with settings
⍝ pairs: vector of (name value) pairs, e.g. ('access_mode' 'READ_ONLY')('threads' '4')
⍝ Returns: config pointer (must be destroyed with destroyConfig)

(st cfg)←api.duckdb_create_config 0
:If st≠0
    cfg←0 ⋄ →0
:EndIf

:For pair :In pairs
    name value←pair
    st←api.duckdb_set_config cfg name value
    :If st≠0
        {}api.duckdb_destroy_config cfg
        cfg←0 ⋄ →0
    :EndIf
:EndFor

⍝ KSL 1.0.0
